What is SRP?

"A class should have one and only one reason to change."
In Swift, this means:
	•	A class or struct should do only one thing.
	•	That “thing” should be clearly defined and cohesive.
	•	If multiple responsibilities exist, they should be split into smaller units.

class UserManager {
    func registerUser(email: String, password: String) {
        // validate
        if email.isEmpty || password.count < 6 {
            print("Invalid input")
            return
        }

        // send network request
        let url = URL(string: "https://example.com/register")!
        var request = URLRequest(url: url)
        request.httpMethod = "POST"
        request.httpBody = try? JSONEncoder().encode(["email": email, "password": password])
        URLSession.shared.dataTask(with: request).resume()

        // save to UserDefaults
        UserDefaults.standard.set(email, forKey: "loggedInUser")
    }
}

