We are seeking a highly skilled Senior iOS Mobile Developer to support the design,
development, and delivery of secure, high-scale mobile applications. This role operates
within KONEK, a fast-moving, startup-style team within an enterprise environment,
contributing to mission-critical initiatives involving secure mobile experiences, API-
driven platforms, and high-reliability systems.
The successful candidate will work closely with product, design, security, and backend
teams and is expected to take strong ownership of technical quality, delivery, and
platform evolution.
Key Responsibilities
• Design, develop, and maintain native iOS applications using Swift and SwiftUI
• Build and maintain SwiftUI-based UI components in a shared design system,
following modern iOS best practices
• Write safe, concurrent code using Swift Concurrency (async/await, actors,
Sendable) under Swift 6 strict concurrency checking
• Implement deep linking and universal links across the app
• Integrate and manage feature flags for controlled rollouts and experimentation
• Collaborate with backend teams to integrate RESTful APIs using secure
communication patterns
• Implement secure authentication and authorization flows, including sign-in with
partner financial institutions
• Ensure applications meet security, performance, availability, accessibility, and
compliance requirements
• Deliver accessible, fully localized experiences (VoiceOver, Dynamic Type,
English and Canadian French)
• Contribute to architecture and technical design decisions, including
modularization (Swift Package Manager) and scalability
• Implement and maintain automated testing (unit, integration, UI) using Swift
Testing, XCTest, and XCUITest, and support CI/CD pipelines
• Take ownership of release management, build pipelines, multi-environment build
configurations, TestFlight, and App Store submissions
• Monitor production health (crash reporting, performance, network errors) and
troubleshoot and resolve production issues with a focus on stability and
resilience
• Participate in code reviews and promote mobile engineering best practices
• Partner with the Android developer to keep features and behaviour consistent
across platforms
• Work independently in a small, high-ownership team environment while
collaborating cross-functionally
Required Qualifications
• 6+ years of professional iOS development experience, including at least one app
shipped and supported in the App Store
• Strong proficiency in Swift, SwiftUI, Swift Concurrency, iOS SDK, and Apple
development frameworks, with working knowledge of UIKit
• Strong understanding of modern iOS architecture patterns (MVVM, Clean
Architecture, Coordinator) and dependency injection
• Hands-on experience with secure mobile development practices (OWASP
MASVS / Mobile Top 10)
• Experience working with the Core Bluetooth framework for scanning, connecting,
and communicating with Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) devices
• Experience integrating backend systems using REST/JSON APIs
• Experience with deep linking, universal links, and feature flagging
• Familiarity with App Store deployment, App Store Connect, provisioning profiles,
and certificates
• Experience working in Agile / Scrum delivery environments
• Comfortable working in a high-ownership, startup-paced team within an
enterprise
Security-Focused Experience (Required)
• Secure authentication mechanisms including biometrics (Face ID / Touch ID) and
secure PIN flows
• Experience with certificate pinning and secure network communication
• Understanding of JWT tokens and secure session management (token refresh,
expiry, and sign-out)
